# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment — never commit real values. NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are the ONLY
# vars this project ever uses; they are safe to ship to the browser by
# design (Supabase anon key + this backend's public URL), never a secret.
.env.local
.env*.local

# src/types/admin-api.d.ts (generated via `npm run generate:api-types`) is
# INTENTIONALLY COMMITTED, not ignored (Phase 13) — a clean CI/deploy
# checkout of only this repo has no access to the sibling backend repo's
# filesystem path the generator reads from, so the build needs this file to
# already be present in git. Anti-drift is enforced from the backend side
# instead: its own CI regenerates docs/admin-openapi.json and fails if that
# diverges from what the zod schemas would produce, and this repo's own
# `npm run typecheck` fails loudly if a stale committed .d.ts stops matching
# how src/lib/api.ts actually uses it. Regenerating and committing the
# result is still a deliberate, manual step after any admin API change.

